Important AOP Terminologies :
1. Aspect : An Aspect is a class that contains AOP logic.
Example:
@Aspect
public class LoggingAspect {}
--> Purpose:
1. Logging
2. Security
3. Transaction
4. Monitoring

2. Advice : Action performed by an Aspect.
Example:
@Before
public void logMethod() {}
Here, logMethod() is Advice.
--> Types of Advice
1. Before Advice : Runs before method execution.
@Before(...)
Example:
Check Login
Check Security
Logging Start
2. After Advice : Runs after method execution.
@After(...)
Example:
Close Connection
Logging End
3. After Returning Advice : Runs only if method succeeds.
@AfterReturning(...)
Example:
Save Success Log
4. After Throwing Advice : Runs only when exception occurs.
@AfterThrowing(...)
Example:
Error Logging
5. Around Advice : Most powerful advice.
Runs:
Before Method AND After Method
Example:
@Around(...)

3. Join Point : A point in application execution where AOP can be applied.
Examples:
1. Method Call
2. Method Execution
3. Exception Throwing
Suppose, saveStudent() --> This method execution is a Join Point.

4. Pointcut : A rule that selects which Join Points should execute Advice.
Example:
@Before("execution(* com.example.service.*.*(..))")
Meaning:
--> Apply to all methods
--> inside service package

Aspect vs Advice :
| Aspect             | Advice               |
| ------------------ | -------------------- |
| Complete AOP class | Method inside Aspect |
| Contains logic     | Actual action        |
| @Aspect            | @Before, @After      |
