Lombok : It is a Java library that automatically generates repetitive code for us.
Instead of writing:
--> Getter Methods
--> Setter Methods
--> Constructors
--> toString()
--> equals()
--> hashCode()
manually, Lombok generates them automatically using annotations.

Code Example :
Student.java--> 

package com.example.model;

import lombok.Getter;
import lombok.Setter;

@Getter
@Setter
public class Student 
{
    private int id;
    private String name;
}

Main Class--> 
package com.example;

import com.example.model.Student;

public class App 
{
    public static void main(String[] args) 
    {
        Student student = new Student();

        student.setId(101);
        student.setName("Teju");

        System.out.println(student.getId());
        System.out.println(student.getName());
    }
}
//student.setId(101); Setter generated by Lombok.
//student.setName("Teju"); Setter generated by Lombok.

Output :
101
Teju
